Video Poker 0.6.6

This independent, offline game's original program code and hardware integration
are GPL-2.0-or-later. See LICENSE. Corresponding source and build instructions
accompany the distributed image. The runtime is adapted from the earlier
SeedSigner Dino launcher and uses the original SeedSigner ST7789/GPIO driver.

Stock SeedSigner 0.8.7, its operating-system components and its fonts retain their
original notices and licenses. The visual asset directory contains card and GUI
artwork from the public VideoPoker.com asset service and rasterized Arial glyphs.
Those images, marks and font-derived bitmaps retain their owners' rights and are
not relicensed under this project's GPL. See THIRD-PARTY-ASSETS.txt and the asset
manifest for per-file sources, hashes and conversions. No raw font outlines,
commercial gameplay source, game ROM, emulator or network service is included.
The independently written game uses virtual credits only.
There is no money-in, cash-out, account or networking. Live game state stays in RAM.
Training history and device preferences may be saved only with explicit opt-in.

The production entrypoint launches Video Poker. Its hidden gesture opens the
trainer and calculator. The underlying OS and display driver remain upstream
components. Physical cold boot, display timing and buttons require testing on
the actual target hardware.

This is an independent community build, not official IGT, Action Gaming,
VideoPoker.com, BitKit or SeedSigner software. Project releases and source:
https://github.com/xberenguer/videopoker .

Original strategy data is generated by exhaustive enumeration and numerical
average-reward optimization. Floating-point certificates do not constitute
formal interval proofs, vendor certification or a guarantee of winning.

